  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Fresh Grocery Counter",
    "overview": "Koelakan reads as a fresh, modern grocery app for warung owners: soft white cards resting on a pale mint ground, one emerald colour that means \"act\" or \"this is live\", and a pastel tint for each of the four staples with cut-out produce imagery on it. Money is the hero of every screen. The signature is the savings strip: the PIHPS market price struck through, the price actually paid in emerald, and a thin bar showing how far below the market it landed.\n\nDensity is calm and phone-first. Cards are generous (20-24px inside), tap targets never drop under 44px, and the structure is one column on a phone that opens into a main column plus a 20-22rem side column on a laptop. The ground carries a faint emerald wash in the top-right corner and a faint sky wash in the bottom-left; everything else is flat colour.\n\nThe world was chosen against two looks it replaces: the dark crypto dashboard and the kraft-paper, nostalgic ledger. Chain detail is present but tucked away under disclosures, so the surface stays a shop tool, not a block explorer.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale mint ground (#eef6f2) with white 20px-radius cards, hairline green-grey border, soft two-layer shadow.",
      "One emerald (#0a7f61) for actions, selection, the savings figure and the agent's live state.",
      "Four staple pastels, each paired with a darker same-hue text tint.",
      "One friendly geometric sans (Figtree) with tabular numerals for every amount, quantity and time.",
      "Lucide stroke icons only; produce raster cut-outs for the four items and the hero.",
      "Status always pairs a colour with a word or icon."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Emerald Rule",
        "body": "Emerald is the only action colour. It marks what to press, what is selected, what was saved and that the agent is alive; it never decorates.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pastel Belongs To Food Rule",
        "body": "Rice, sugar, eggs and oil pastels appear only where that item is the subject (its card, its image disc). They are never used for states, sections or generic decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Word With Every Colour Rule",
        "body": "A status colour always ships with text or a drawn icon: chips carry a dot plus a word, notices carry an icon, the savings bar carries \"x% below PIHPS\".",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every rupiah amount, quantity, round number and clock time is set with tabular numerals (`.num`: tnum, -0.005em) so columns and before/after prices align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels, chips and table heads are sentence case at normal tracking. Hierarchy is weight and size, not capitals or letter-spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Panel Rule",
        "body": "A panel is never nested inside another panel. Inside a card, group with hairline dividers, a mint inset (ground or brand-soft) or spacing.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Only For Chrome Rule",
        "body": "Backdrop blur appears only on the fixed navigation (rail at 90% white, tab bar at 95% white), never on content.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep emerald (#0a7f61) for actions, selection, the paid price and live state; use Mint Wash (#e3f4ee) for selected fills.",
      "Do show a saving as the savings strip: PIHPS struck, paid in emerald, bar, \"% below PIHPS\".",
      "Do set every amount, quantity and time with tabular numerals.",
      "Do keep tap targets at 44px or more (56px in the tab bar) and keep the 3px emerald focus outline.",
      "Do pair every status colour with a word or a drawn stroke icon.",
      "Do turn wide tables into stacked label/value rows on phones.",
      "Do keep motion short and from a visible default: 150-200ms ease-out for state, a 240ms rise for arriving live data, and honour reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't drift toward the dark crypto dashboard or the kraft-paper, nostalgic ledger look this world replaces.",
      "Don't use the item pastels for anything other than their item.",
      "Don't nest a white panel inside another panel.",
      "Don't introduce a second typeface, uppercase tracked labels, or a second icon library.",
      "Don't use hard offset shadows or heavy lifts; modals are the only Lift.",
      "Don't put raw chain detail (hashes, tx payloads) in the first read; reveal it in a disclosure."
    ]
  }
}